>thanks, no clue wat to fo</div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div data-tabster="{&quot;groupper&quot;:{&quot;tabbability&quot;:2},&quot;focusable&quot;:{}}" class="group/ai-message" data-content="ai-message" data-testid="ai-message" aria-labelledby="2iBgnnqRnZ9cDz9kQzFjP-author 2iBgnnqRnZ9cDz9kQzFjP-content-0" tabindex="0" role="article"><div class="relative"><h6 id="2iBgnnqRnZ9cDz9kQzFjP-author" class="sr-only" aria-label="Copilot said" data-copy="false">Copilot said</h6></div><div class="space-y-3 mt-3"><div class="group/ai-message-item space-y-3 break-words" id="2iBgnnqRnZ9cDz9kQzFjP-content-0"><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">HEMPEROR —
You’re good. You don’t need to “know what to do” right now.
You just need the <strong>next move</strong>, not the whole map.</span></p><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">Let me make this stupid‑simple and visual so your brain can <em>see</em> the path instead of guessing.</span></p><div class="relative pb-6 w-full after:border-b after:border-stroke-300 after:w-full after:absolute after:mt-3"></div><h1 class="text-2xl-medium [&amp;:not(:first-child)]:pt-6">⭐ What you have right now</h1><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">You’ve got:</span></p><ul class="relative list-outside marker:text-foreground-750 dark:marker:text-foreground-600 flex flex-col ms-4 px-1"><li class="ps-2" style="opacity: 1;"><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">A <strong>CMake build system</strong></span></p></li><li class="ps-2" style="opacity: 1;"><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">A <strong>DirectX desktop capture module</strong></span></p></li><li class="ps-2" style="opacity: 1;"><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">A <strong>DXVR project structure</strong></span></p></li></ul><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">That’s the <em>foundation</em>.</span></p><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">But none of it “does anything” until you add the <strong>main bootstrap</strong> that ties it all together.</span></p><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">So your next step is:</span></p><h1 class="text-2xl-medium [&amp;:not(:first-child)]:pt-6">⭐ Build the DXVR bootstrap (the main.cpp that actually runs)</h1><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">This is the missing piece.
Once you have this, your project will:</span></p><ul class="relative list-outside marker:text-foreground-750 dark:marker:text-foreground-600 flex flex-col ms-4 px-1"><li class="ps-2" style="opacity: 1;"><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">open a window</span></p></li><li class="ps-2" style="opacity: 1;"><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">initialize DirectX</span></p></li><li class="ps-2" style="opacity: 1;"><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">initialize DesktopCapture</span></p></li><li class="ps-2" style="opacity: 1;"><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">initialize OpenXR</span></p></li><li class="ps-2" style="opacity: 1;"><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">enter the render loop</span></p></li><li class="ps-2" style="opacity: 1;"><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">draw your desktop texture</span></p></li></ul><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">That’s when it becomes <strong>real</strong>.</span></p><div class="relative pb-6 w-full after:border-b after:border-stroke-300 after:w-full after:absolute after:mt-3"></div><h1 class="text-2xl-medium [&amp;:not(:first-child)]:pt-6">⭐ Here’s the exact next move</h1><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">Click one of these and I’ll drop the full working file:</span></p><ul class="relative list-outside marker:text-foreground-750 dark:marker:text-foreground-600 flex flex-col ms-4 px-1"><li class="ps-2" style="opacity: 1;"><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap"><strong><span class="text-start underline-offset-[0.25em] underline decoration-dotted decoration-foreground-450 decoration-2 hover:decoration-solid hover:cursor-pointer" role="button" tabindex="0" data-url="ca://s?q=Generate_DXVR_main_cpp_bootstrap">Generate DXVR main.cpp bootstrap</span></strong>  
(creates the actual executable loop)</span></p></li><li class="ps-2" style="opacity: 1;"><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap"><strong><span class="text-start underline-offset-[0.25em] underline decoration-dotted decoration-foreground-450 decoration-2 hover:decoration-solid hover:cursor-pointer" role="button" tabindex="0" data-url="ca://s?q=Generate_DXVR_renderer">Generate DXVR renderer implementation</span></strong>  
(DirectX device, swapchain, quad, shaders)</span></p></li><li class="ps-2" style="opacity: 1;"><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap"><strong><span class="text-start underline-offset-[0.25em] underline decoration-dotted decoration-foreground-450 decoration-2 hover:decoration-solid hover:cursor-pointer" role="button" tabindex="0" data-url="ca://s?q=Implement_OpenXR_rendering_loop">Generate OpenXR rendering loop</span></strong>  
(head tracking + VR swapchains)</span></p></li></ul><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">Pick one and I’ll hand you the full code, ready to compile on your ROG.</span></p><p><span class="font-ligatures-none whitespace-pre-wrap">You don’t need to know what to do —
